# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone on Windows
# rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF in the working tree. Git Bash's bash
# tolerates a CRLF shebang, so bootstrap happens to survive that - but nothing
# else in the toolchain promises to. WSL bash, /usr/bin/env, node shebangs and
# the git hooks under githooks/ all fail on a stray ^M, and a machine that
# switches between native Windows and WSL against the same ~/.config would hit
# it immediately.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf per file, so this holds regardless of how any
# individual machine is configured. It also keeps diffs free of whole-file
# rewrites when the same repo is edited from more than one platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png     binary
*.icns    binary
*.ico     binary
*.zip     binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
